1
00:00:00,960 --> 00:00:05,340
Every map app answers one
question. What's fastest?

2
00:00:05,990 --> 00:00:07,910
But when you're walking home at night,

3
00:00:07,950 --> 00:00:10,170
that's not the question
you're really asking.

4
00:00:10,954 --> 00:00:15,794
In Atlanta, pedestrian crashes pile
up on a small share of streets,

5
00:00:15,834 --> 00:00:19,344
and the risk rises and falls
with the hour and the weather.

6
00:00:19,454 --> 00:00:22,204
My friends already plan
around it by instinct:

7
00:00:22,244 --> 00:00:26,274
well-lit streets, busier streets,
texting when they get home.

8
00:00:26,984 --> 00:00:29,154
Nobody had built a map for that.

9
00:00:29,702 --> 00:00:31,762
I'm Nagur Shareef Shaik.

10
00:00:31,802 --> 00:00:34,842
I built PathPro, solo, this weekend.

11
00:00:35,350 --> 00:00:39,250
Open pathpro.tech. No app, no account.

12
00:00:39,290 --> 00:00:42,540
Two taps, and you get a route
that costs four extra minutes

13
00:00:42,580 --> 00:00:46,370
and cuts your traffic-risk
exposure by fifty-four percent.

14
00:00:46,780 --> 00:00:48,400
Then it walks with you.

15
00:00:48,568 --> 00:00:50,328
<i>High traffic risk ahead.</i>

16
00:00:50,368 --> 00:00:55,388
<i>Fowler Street Northwest and Ferst</i>
<i>Drive Northwest, in 300 meters.</i>

17
00:00:55,644 --> 00:00:58,144
Eyes on the street, not the screen.

18
00:00:58,542 --> 00:01:00,502
Tap any street to see why.

19
00:01:00,542 --> 00:01:05,812
The factors add up exactly to the score,
and Grok explains it in plain words.

20
00:01:05,852 --> 00:01:08,272
But Grok can't invent a single number:

21
00:01:08,312 --> 00:01:12,742
if a sentence isn't backed by the
evidence, it never reaches your screen.

22
00:01:13,192 --> 00:01:17,672
Riding? Bike, e-bike and scooter
get their own crash model:

23
00:01:17,712 --> 00:01:21,722
seventy-one percent less traffic
risk for four extra minutes.

24
00:01:21,762 --> 00:01:24,612
Long walk? It hands you off to MARTA.

25
00:01:25,030 --> 00:01:30,490
After dark, choose well-lit, busier
streets, with help points along the way.

26
00:01:30,570 --> 00:01:35,260
Share your walk with a friend, and if
you're running late, PathPro checks in.

27
00:01:35,300 --> 00:01:39,180
Reported crimes are shown for
context, with a fairness note,

28
00:01:39,220 --> 00:01:41,690
and they never, ever choose your route.

29
00:01:42,146 --> 00:01:48,206
And for the people who fix streets:
tap "Imagine this street redesigned".

30
00:01:48,246 --> 00:01:52,316
Grok Imagine draws the fixes
this exact street needs,

31
00:01:52,356 --> 00:01:55,946
like crosswalks, curb
extensions and lighting.

32
00:01:56,016 --> 00:01:59,436
Then Gemini checks the
picture before anyone sees it.

33
00:01:59,476 --> 00:02:02,666
See the change before a
dollar is spent on concrete.

34
00:02:03,162 --> 00:02:05,762
Still curious? Ask PathPro.

35
00:02:05,842 --> 00:02:10,892
Built on Backboard, it answers from my
model's own documents and whatever street,

36
00:02:10,932 --> 00:02:13,032
route or area you're looking at.

37
00:02:13,072 --> 00:02:16,332
Turn on memory and it remembers
how you like to travel.

38
00:02:16,372 --> 00:02:18,682
Tap Forget me, and it's gone.

39
00:02:19,290 --> 00:02:20,410
Does it work?

40
00:02:20,450 --> 00:02:27,690
I trained on 2020 to 2023 and tested
on 2024, a year the model never saw.

41
00:02:27,750 --> 00:02:30,520
The ten percent of
streets PathPro flags held

42
00:02:30,560 --> 00:02:33,420
seventy-four percent
of pedestrian crashes.

43
00:02:33,480 --> 00:02:36,890
The City's own High Injury
Network? Fifty-four.

44
00:02:37,700 --> 00:02:41,590
Same budget, about thirty-eight
percent more crashes reached.

45
00:02:42,050 --> 00:02:46,960
It runs on Vultr in Atlanta,
keeps working when any service fails,

46
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:49,830
and its demo mode even works offline.

47
00:02:51,286 --> 00:02:55,526
Mission control for
every walk home. PathPro.

48
00:02:55,656 --> 00:02:59,036
See the risks on your way, before you go.
